:: Balloon Stand [exitCheckBypass]
<<clearsinglenpc 0>><<loadNPC 0 "stall_owner">><<person1>>

<div id="clothingShop-div" class="main-shop-div">
	<<stallShop-main>>
</div>

:: Balloon Purchase
<<effects>>
<<if $balloonStand.owner is "angry" and ["hot cocoa", "hot cider", "cold drink"].includes($phase)>>
	The <<person>> regards you for a long moment before sighing. "Sure," <<he>> says, sounding resigned. "Look, I'm sorry for losing my cool. It was kind of a dick move to start selling my own drinks after promising to help, but to be fair, you hurt me after you promised to get me off. I don't like being angry, though. We're good, right?"
	<br><br>
	<<He>> has a point. You nod. "We're good."
	<<set $balloonStand.owner to "appeased">>
<<else>>
	<<set _sir to playerPronoun() is "m" ? "sir" : playerPronoun() is "f" ? "miss" : "Mx">>
	"<<print $balloonStand.owner is "angry" ? "Sure, whatever," : either("Certainly,", "Right away, _sir,", "Sure thing,", "Coming right up,", "Absolutely!")>>" the <<person>> says.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<switch $phase>>
	<<case "popcorn">>
		<<He>> scoops out some freshly-popped popcorn. The bag's still warm when <<he>> hands it to you.
		<<set $daily.ex.popcorn to ($daily.ex.popcorn or 0) + 1>>
		<<wearProp "popcorn">>

		<<if $daily.ex.popcorn is 2 and $balloonStand.owner isnot "angry">>
			"You must be hungry," <<he>> says. <<print playerBellyVisible() ? `"I suppose you are eating for two." <<He>> smiles, glancing affectionately at your baby bump.` : `"Not getting enough to eat at home?" <<His>> brow creases momentarily, but <<he>> quickly shakes it off.`>>
		<<elseif $daily.ex.popcorn is 3>>
			"Gotta save some for the other customers, so I'm gonna have to cut you off after this." <<print $balloonStand.owner is "angry" ? "<<His>> voice is curt" : "<<He>> gives you an apologetic smile">>.
		<</if>>
	<<default>>
		<<set $daily.ex.balloonDrink to ($daily.ex.balloonDrink or 0) + 1>>
		<<switch $phase2>>
			<<case "hotcocoa">>
				<<wearProp "travel cup">>
			<<case "strawberrylemonade">>
				<<wearProp "strawberry lemonade">>
			<<case "hotcider">>
				<<wearProp "travel cup cider">>
			<<default>>
				<<wearProp "lemonade">>
		<</switch>>

		<<if $phase is "cold drink">>
			<<He>> pours you a glass of ice-cold <<seasonal_beverage>>. The plastic cup sweats in your hand.
		<<else>>
			<<He>> pours you a cup of steaming <<seasonal_beverage>>. The paper cup warms your hands.
		<</if>>

		<<if $daily.ex.balloonDrink is 2>>
			"Thirsty, eh?" <<he>> says. "<<print playerBellyVisible() ? "Guess you gotta keep that little one hydrated, too" : "Glad to see you're staying hydrated">>." <<He>> smiles at you.
		<<elseif $daily.ex.balloonDrink is 3>>
			"Gotta save some for the other customers, so I'm gonna have to cut you off after this." <<He>> gives you an apologetic smile.
		<</if>>
<</switch>>
"<<print $balloonStand.owner is "angry" ? "There you go. Get lost." : either("Good to see you, love.", "Have a great rest of your day now.", "Thanks for your custom.", "Enjoy!")>>"
<br><br>
<<switch $phase>>
	<<case "popcorn">>
		<<link [[Eat the popcorn (0:15)|Balloon Consume]]>><<set $phase to $balloonStand.robin.status is "help needed" ? "ask_eat" : "popcorn">><<trauma -3>><</link>><<ltrauma>><br>
		<<if $balloonStand.robin.status is "help needed">>
			<<link [[Save it for later|Balloon Consume]]>><<set $phase to "ask">> <<set $popcorn += 1>><</link>><br>
		<<else>>
			<<link [[Save it for later|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<set $popcorn += 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
		<</if>>
	<<default>>
		<<link [[Take a sip (0:15)|Balloon Consume]]>><<stress -9>><<pass 15>><</link>><<lstress>><br>
<</switch>>

:: Balloon Consume
<<effects>>

<<switch $phase>>
	<<case "cold drink">>You take a sip. The <<seasonal_beverage>> is <<print Time.season is "spring" ? "pleasantly fruity" : "tart">> and refreshing, and you can feel the stress melting away.
	<<case "popcorn" "park" "ask_eat">>You pop a handful of popcorn into your mouth. It's buttery and salty, and it brings back nostalgic memories of trips to the cinema.
	<<case "ask">>You fold over the top of the bag so popcorn doesn't spill everywhere before pocketing it.
	<<default>>You take a careful sip, careful not to scald your tongue. The <<seasonal_beverage>> is rich <<print Time.season is "winter" ? "and creamy" : "with spices">>, and you can feel the stress melting away.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<if ["ask","ask_eat"].includes($phase)>>
	"I've been meaning to ask," the <<person>> says, resting <<his>> elbows on the stall as <<he>> leans over to chat with you. "What do you think of the popcorn? Good, right?"
	<br><br>
	<<speechresolve>>
	<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
		<<case "meek">>
			You clutch the bag a little tighter before answering. "It's very good, <<sir>>," you tell <<him>> softly. "Although, um... it is kind of salty?"
		<<case "shy">>
			You glance down at the popcorn, then back up at <<him>>. "It is good," you admit, almost under your breath. "Maybe just a little salty."
		<<case "polite">>
			You offer <<him>> an apologetic smile. "It's very tasty. If I had one suggestion, it might be to go a little lighter on the salt."
		<<case "flamboyant">>
			You flash <<him>> a bright smile and lift the bag slightly in demonstration. "Delicious, darling. A touch dramatic on the salt, perhaps, but certainly memorable."
		<<case "docile">>
			You nod obediently and answer when prompted. "It's good. Maybe a little salty, but I like it."
		<<case "confident">>
			You give the popcorn another thoughtful bite before replying. "Yeah, it's good. Bit heavy on the salt, though. Makes people thirsty."
		<<case "bratty">>
			You smack your lips and grin at <<him>>. "Yeah, gotta admit, you did good with it. Salty, though. I'm parched."
		<<case "cruel">>
			You tip the bag in <<his>> direction with a sharp little look. "Good enough to sell, sure, but you really laid the salt on thick. Makes it a bit obvious what you're doing."
		<<default>>
			You give an appreciative nod. "It's tasty, yeah. If I had to critique it, it's a bit salty, though."
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>
	"Salt is addictive. That's how you keep 'em coming back," <<he>> says with a wink. "But good to know. I'm always open to ways to improve."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Suggest that the stall owner partner with Robin|Balloon Partner]]>><<set $phase to "help">><</link>><br>
	<<link [[Suggest that the stall owner sell beverages|Balloon Partner]]>><<set $phase to "sabotage">><</link>>
<<elseif $phase is "park">>
	<<link [[Next|Park]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Balloon Partner
<<effects>>
<<location "beach">><<npc Robin 2>><<person2>>
<<set _boyfriend to ($robinromance ? `<<nnpc_girlfriend "Robin">>` : "friend")>>

<<switch $phase>>
	<<case "help">>
		<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
			<<case "meek">>
				You clear your throat and bring the suggestion up as gently as you can.
			<<case "shy">>
				You linger a moment before broaching the subject, choosing your words with care.
			<<case "polite">>
				You smooth over the transition with an easy, courteous smile before making your suggestion.
			<<case "flamboyant">>
				You lean in like you're about to reveal a marvelous little secret.
			<<case "docile">>
				You wait for a lull in the conversation, then offer the idea in a mild, careful tone.
			<<case "confident">>
				You step in like you've already thought the arrangement through from every angle.
			<<case "bratty">>
				You grin, already half-convinced you've spotted an obvious business opportunity for <<person1>><<him>>.
			<<case "cruel">>
				You angle the conversation where you want it with brisk, unsentimental precision.
			<<default>>
				You decide to bring up the idea while <<person1>><<he>> still seems open to listening.
		<</switch>>
		<br><br>
		<<person2>>
		<<if getRobinLocation() is "beach">>
			"My _boyfriend's selling lemonade, right across the way there." You nod at Robin's lemonade stand. "It's really tasty. I think your customers would appreciate a nice cold drink after some of your popcorn."
		<<else>>
			"<<print Time.season is "winter" ? "When it's not cold out," : "<<Hes>> not there right now, but">> my _boyfriend spends the weekend selling lemonade, right across the way there. You've probably seen <<him>> around." You nod at the spot where Robin normally sets up shop. "<<print Time.season is "winter" ? "Now that it's winter, <<hes>> selling hot cocoa over in the park." : "It's really tasty.">> I think it'd hit the spot after some of your popcorn."
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		The <<person1>><<person>> cocks <<his>> head, considering your words.
		<<if C.npc.Robin.crossdressing gte 2 and getRobinLocation() is "beach" and $robinromance>>
			"<<print (_boyfriend.toUpperFirst())>>?" <<He>> glances at Robin's <<= C.npc.Robin.pronoun is "f" ? "bound chest" : "<<npcClothesText statusCheck('Robin') 'upper'>>">>. "Could've fooled me. Well, whatever gets your jollies, eh?" <<He>> gives you a wry smile before continuing.
			<<set _boyfriend to C.npc.Robin.pronoun is "f" ? "'Girlfriend'" : "'Boyfriend'">>
		<</if>>
		"I've tried that lemonade of <<person2>><<hers>> before," <<person1>><<he>> says. "It's mostly sugar water. I'm not saying no, but you're gonna have to work a little harder to convince me that partnering with your little _boyfriend isn't a terrible idea."
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Persuade|Balloon Convince]]>><<set $phase to "persuade">><</link>><<englishdifficulty 1 1000>><br>
		<<if hasSexStat("promiscuity", 4)>>
			<<link [[Seduce|Balloon Convince]]>><<set $phase to "seduce">><</link>><<promiscuous4>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<if setup.inflation.canAfford(30000, "bribe")>>
			<<link [[Bribe (<<printprice 30000>>)|Balloon Convince]]>><<set $phase to "bribe">><<money -30000 "bribe">><</link>>
		<</if>>

	<<case "sabotage">>
		<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
			<<case "meek">>
				You bring it up as though you're only half-sure you should. "Have you considered selling beverages alongside your popcorn?"
			<<case "shy">>
				You steal a quick breath before speaking. "Have you thought about selling drinks too?"
			<<case "polite">>
				You tilt your head toward the stand. "Have you considered offering beverages alongside your popcorn?"
			<<case "flamboyant">>
				You gesture grandly at the stall. "Darling, have you considered expanding into beverages to complete the experience?"
			<<case "docile">>
				You wait for the right moment, then quietly make your suggestion. "Have you considered selling beverages alongside your popcorn?"
			<<case "confident">>
				You cut straight to the point. "You should think about selling drinks with the popcorn. Have you considered it?"
			<<case "bratty">>
				You grin like you're handing over a clever little trick. "Ever think about selling drinks with the popcorn too?"
			<<case "cruel">>
				You glance over the stall with clinical interest. "You'd make more money if you sold drinks as well. Considered that?"
			<<default>>
				"Have you considered selling beverages alongside your popcorn?" you ask.
		<</switch>>
		<br><br>
		The <<person1>><<person>> hums noncommittally as <<he>> wipes down <<his>> stand. "Like your buddy <<print getRobinLocation() is "beach" ? "over there" : Time.season is "winter" ? "who sells hot chocolate in the park" : "who sells lemonade">>?" <<He>> leans in conspiratorially. "I've tried <<person2>><<his>> lemonade before. <<Hes>> a bit heavy-handed on the sugar, and really ought to invest in a proper juicer."
		<br><br>
		<<person1>><<He>> straightens back up. "What does your friend charge, anyway?" <<he>> muses, glancing over at <<print getRobinLocation() is "beach" ? "Robin's stall" : "where Robin normally sets up shop">>. "A pound? You can't make a living like that. Who knows, maybe a little friendly rivalry will help drum up some business for <<person2>><<him>>." The <<person1>><<person>> chuckles. "I'm already thinking of a seasonal menu. Cider in the fall, strawberry lemonade in the spring... this'll be fun. Stop by tomorrow, why don't you? I'll give you a drink on the house." <<set $balloonStand.freeDrink to true>>
		<br><br>
		<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
			<<case "meek">>
				"That's very kind of you, <<sir>>." You give <<him>> a small, grateful smile. "Thank you."
			<<case "shy">>
				You brighten a little despite yourself. "Oh. Thank you," you say, the words coming out softer than you intended.
			<<case "polite">>
				"That's very generous of you." You smile warmly. "Thank you."
			<<case "flamboyant">>
				You lift a hand to your chest in pleased surprise. "A complimentary drink? You do know how to flatter, darling. Thank you."
			<<case "docile">>
				You nod and accept the offer without fuss. "Thank you. That's kind of you."
			<<case "confident">>
				You grin back at <<him>>. "I like the sound of that. Thanks."
			<<case "bratty">>
				"Sure, sign me up." You grin. "I'm always down for a freebie."
			<<case "cruel">>
				You give <<him>> a cool, satisfied look. "Sensibly done. I'll take you up on it."
			<<default>>
				"I'd like that very much." You smile. "Thank you."
		<</switch>>
	<br><br>
	"Don't expect me to make a habit of it, though. I gotta earn a living here," <<he>> says with a wink. "You know, you're a shrewd one, <<girl>>. Keep it up, and you'll make a fine business magnate someday." <<stress -6>><<lstress>>
	<<balloonRobinSabotaged>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</switch>>

:: Balloon Convince
<<effects>>
<<npc Robin 2>><<person1>>
<<speechresolve>>

<<switch $phase>>
	<<case "persuade">>
		<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
			<<case "meek">>
				You wring your hands a little as you speak, piling praise onto Robin's <<print Time.season is "winter" ? "hot chocolate" : "lemonade">> and carefully nudging the conversation toward sympathy. For good measure, you bring up Robin's history as an orphan.
			<<case "shy">>
				You speak at length about Robin's <<print Time.season is "winter" ? "hot chocolate" : "lemonade">>, gaining momentum as you go. By the end, you're gently appealing to the stall owner's better nature and mentioning Robin's rough upbringing.
			<<case "polite">>
				You make your case with patient courtesy, praising Robin's <<print Time.season is "winter" ? "hot chocolate" : "lemonade">> and neatly framing the partnership as mutually beneficial. You even slip in a softened version of Robin's history as an orphan.
			<<case "flamboyant">>
				You turn the pitch into a performance, praising Robin's <<print Time.season is "winter" ? "hot chocolate" : "lemonade">> with theatrical enthusiasm and painting the whole thing as a charming collaboration. For extra effect, you invoke Robin's tragic little orphan backstory.
			<<case "docile">>
				You explain the idea as clearly and obediently as you can, focusing on Robin's <<print Time.season is "winter" ? "hot chocolate" : "lemonade">> and how well it would pair with the popcorn. In the end, you quietly mention Robin's past to tug at the stall owner's heart.
			<<case "confident">>
				You lay out the arrangement like a business plan: Robin's <<print Time.season is "winter" ? "hot chocolate" : "lemonade">>, <<person1>><<his>> popcorn, shared foot traffic, shared profit. When that alone doesn't feel like enough, you add Robin's orphan history for emotional weight.
			<<case "bratty">>
				You sell the idea with a quick grin and plenty of nerve, talking up Robin's <<print Time.season is "winter" ? "hot chocolate" : "lemonade">> before throwing in a sob story about Robin growing up an orphan to really twist the knife.
			<<case "cruel">>
				You present the whole arrangement with cold efficiency, praising Robin's <<print Time.season is "winter" ? "hot chocolate" : "lemonade">> only as much as necessary before weaponising Robin's orphan history for leverage.
			<<default>>
				You talk at length about the virtues of Robin's <<print Time.season is "winter" ? "hot chocolate" : "lemonade">>. For good measure, you spin up a sob story about Robin's history as an orphan.
		<</switch>>
		<br><br>
		<<if $englishSuccess>>
			<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
				<<case "meek">>
					"You'd really be helping <<person2>><<him>> out, <<person1>><<sir>>," you say, eyes wide and earnest. "<<person2>><<Hes>> a good person, and <<he>> just needs someone to cut <<him>> a break for once. And it would help you too, I promise."
				<<case "shy">>
					You gather your nerve and press on. "<<person2>><<Hes>> a good person," you say. "<<He>> just needs somebody to give <<him>> a chance. I really think the arrangement could work for both of you."
				<<case "polite">>
					"You'd be doing <<person2>><<him>> a real kindness," you say. "<<He>>'d gladly send customers your way as well. I genuinely think it would benefit both of you."
				<<case "flamboyant">>
					You spread your hands as though unveiling the perfect solution. "Think of it, darling: thirsty customers for <<person2>><<him>>, hungry customers for you, and a little generosity making everyone look marvelous."
				<<case "docile">>
					"<<person2>><<Hes>> trying very hard," you say quietly. "If you help <<him>>, <<he>>'ll help you back. It could be good for both of you."
				<<case "confident">>
					"This is good business," you tell <<person1>><<him>>. "<<person2>><<He>> gets thirsty customers, you get hungry ones, and both of you look better for it. Everybody wins."
				<<case "bratty">>
					"Come on, it's obvious," you say. "<<person2>><<He>> sends thirsty people your way, you send hungry ones <<his>> way, and you get to play generous while making money off it."
				<<case "cruel">>
					"It's a cheap way to buy goodwill and extra customers at the same time," you say flatly. "You help <<person2>><<him>>, <<he>> repays the favour, and everyone acts like you're a saint."
				<<default>>
					"You'd really be helping <<person2>><<him>> out, <<person1>><<sir>>," you say, eyes wide and earnest. <<person2>>"<<Hes>> a good person, and <<he>> just needs someone to cut <<him>> a break for once. And it will be a two-way street, I assure you. <<He>>'ll happily send customers your way as well. Plus, think of all the good karma you'll be racking up, helping an unfortunate orphan get a leg up in this cruel world!"
			<</switch>>
			<br><br>
			The <<person1>><<person>> looks moved by your passionate words. <<balloonRobinHelped>>
			<br><br>
			<<link [[Next|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
		<<else>>
			The <<person1>><<person>> looks unmoved. "So, the <<person2>><<personssimple>> had a rough life. Who hasn't? I'm not providing a charity service here, and I don't see what <<he>> has to offer that will benefit me."
			<br><br>
			<<person1>><<He>> sighs. "Look, I'm not an asshole," the <<personsimple>> says. "I'm not convinced, but I like you. Stop by the stall some other time, and I'd be happy to hear you out."
			<<set $daily.ex.balloonConvince to 1>>
			<<set $balloonStand.robin.status to "convince">>
			<br><br>
			<<link [[Next|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
		<</if>>

	<<case "seduce">>
		<<set $seductiondifficulty to 8000>>
		<<seductioncheck>>
		<<seductionskilluptext>>
		<<seductionskilluse>>

		<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
			<<case "meek">>
				You lean over <<person1>><<his>> stall with visible hesitation, then let your voice drop anyway. "Are you sure I can't convince you?" you ask. "I could... use my mouth, if you'd like."
			<<case "shy">>
				You wet your lips and force yourself to hold <<his>> gaze. "Are you sure I can't persuade you another way?" you murmur, leaning a little closer. "I'm good with my mouth."
			<<case "polite">>
				You lower your voice and lean across the stall, smiling as though making a perfectly reasonable offer. "Are you sure there's no arrangement we could come to? I'm very good with my mouth."
			<<case "flamboyant">>
				You lean over the stall with a teasing smile and let the implication hang in the air. "Darling, are you quite sure I can't persuade you? I do have a very talented mouth."
			<<case "docile">>
				You bow your head slightly, then glance up through your lashes. "If talking won't do it... maybe I could convince you another way. I'm very good with my mouth."
			<<case "confident">>
				You lean over the stall like you already know the effect you're having. "Are you sure I can't convince you?" you purr. "I'm very good with my mouth. I'm sure we can come to an agreement."
			<<case "bratty">>
				You lick your lips and glance pointedly at <<his>> crotch. "Are you sure I can't convince you? I'm very good with my mouth. I'm sure we can come to an agreement."
			<<case "cruel">>
				You hold <<his>> gaze and make the offer with chilling certainty. "You can stop pretending you're above it. Let me under the stall and I'll make it worth your while."
			<<default>>
				"Are you sure I can't convince you?" you purr, leaning over <<person1>><<his>> stall. You lick your lips and glance pointedly at <<his>> crotch. "I am very good with my mouth... I'm sure we can come to an agreement."
		<</switch>> <<promiscuity4>>

		<<if $seductionrating gte $seductionrequired>>
			<<He>> looks conflicted for a moment, but relents. "Ah, alright." <<He>> glances around quickly, then ushers you under the stall. "Make good use of that mouth, and I'll help you out. Hurry, before someone sees. I think I spot some potential customers over there."
			<br><br>
			<<link [[Next|Balloon Sex]]>><<set $sexstart to 1>><</link>>
		<<else>>
			The <<person>> looks at you and bursts into laughter, leaving you self-conscious. "Not a chance, sorry. Look, I'm not an asshole," <<he>> says. "I'm not interested, but I like you. Stop by the stall again tomorrow, and I'd be happy to hear you out. Use your words next time, not... whatever this was." <<He>> chuckles to <<himself>> and waves you off.
			<<set $daily.ex.balloonConvince to 1>>
			<<set $balloonStand.robin.status to "convince">>
			<br><br>
			<<link [[Next|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
		<</if>>

	<<case "bribe">>
		<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
			<<case "meek">>
				You fumble the notes out with slightly shaky hands. "M-might this help sweeten the deal?" you ask, offering <<person1>><<him>> <<printprice 30000>>.
			<<case "shy">>
				You avoid <<his>> eyes as you count out the money. "Would this help?" you ask quietly, handing over the <<printprice 30000>>.
			<<case "polite">>
				You count out <<printprice 30000>> and offer it with practiced calm. "Might this help sweeten the deal?"
			<<case "flamboyant">>
				You fan out the notes with a playful flourish before presenting them. "Perhaps a little financial encouragement, darling?" you ask.
			<<case "docile">>
				You count out the money without argument and place it in <<his>> hand. "Would this help convince you?"
			<<case "confident">>
				You count out the money and slide it across as though closing a negotiation. "How about <<printprice 30000>>? Does that do it?"
			<<case "bratty">>
				"Money talks, yeah? How's 300 quid sound?" You count out the money and stuff it in <<person1>><<his>> hands.
			<<case "cruel">>
				You press the notes into <<his>> hand with a cool expression. "There. <<printprice 30000>>. That should be enough to sharpen your judgment."
			<<default>>
				"Would 300 quid convince you?" You count out the money and hand it to <<person1>><<him>>.
		<</switch>>
		<br><br>
		<<He>> pockets the money, looking impressed. <<balloonRobinHelped>>
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Next|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</switch>>

:: Balloon Sex

<<if $sexstart is 1>>
	<<set $sexstart to 0>>
	<<set $enemyno to 1>><<set $enemynomax to 1>>
	<<consensual>>
	<<set $consensual to 1>>
	<<neutral 1>>

	<<person1>><<maninit>>
	You crawl under the stall and give <<him>> a teasing lick.
	<<promiscuity4>><<npcoral>><<set $NPCList[0].mouth to "none">>
	<<set $enemytrust += 10>>
<</if>>
<<effects>>
The <<personsimple>> chats up a customer, doing <<his>> best to keep <<his>> voice steady.
<<effectsman>>
<<man>>
<<stateman>>
<br><br>
<<actionsman>>

<<if _combatend>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Balloon Sex Finish]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Balloon Sex]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<</if>>

:: Balloon Sex Finish
<<location "beach">><<person1>><<effects>>

<<if $enemypleasure gte $enemypleasuremax>>
	<<ejaculation>>
	<<He>> pants as <<he>> comes down from <<his>> orgasm. <<He>> gives your cheek a clumsy pat, and you crawl out from underneath the stall, wiping your mouth.
	<br><br>
	<<balloonRobinHelped>>
<<elseif $enemyhealth lte 0>>
	"Ow, you fucking whore!" the <<person>> shouts, kicking you away from <<him>>. You scramble out from under the stall. "You can forget about me helping your little friend!" <<he>> shouts after you as you sprint away from the stand. "In fact, <span class="red">I'm gonna start selling my own lemonade</span>! Next time, don't bite the hand that feeds you, asshole."

	<<balloonRobinSabotaged "angry">>
<<else>>
	<<encounterEndViolence>>
	<<He>> looks disappointed as you crawl out from the stand. "Was that supposed to convince me?" <<He>> shakes <<his>> head. "Look, I like you. Stop by the stall some other time, and I'm willing to hear you out. Use your words next time, not... whatever this was." <<He>> waves you off.
	<<set $balloonStand.robin.status to "convince">>
	<<set $daily.ex.balloonConvince to 1>>
<</if>>
<<clotheson>>
<<endcombat>>
<<link [[Next|Beach]]>><</link>>

:: Balloon Robin Check-In
<<effects>>
<<loadNPC 0 "stall_owner">><<npc Robin 2>>
<<set $balloonStand.robin.talked to true>>
<<set $balloonStand.robin.knows to ($phase is "confess_helped" or $phase is "confess_sabotaged" ? true : false)>>
<<set _lemonade to Time.season is "winter" ? "hot chocolate" : "lemonade">>
<<set _botchedHelp to ["angry", "appeased"].includes($balloonStand.owner)>>
<<speechresolve>>

<<switch $phase>>
	<<case "confess_helped">>
		<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
			<<case "meek">>
				You rock on your heels, unable to keep the secret to yourself for another second. "W-well," you say, a shy little smile slipping through, "I might know what's causing it..." Robin looks at you with wide eyes as you confess that you convinced the <<person1>><<personsimple>> selling popcorn to send thirsty customers <<his>> way.
			<<case "shy">>
				You duck your head, but the excitement in you wins out. "I think I know why," you admit. "I talked to that <<person1>><<personsimple>> who sells popcorn and asked <<him>> to send thirsty customers over here."
			<<case "polite">>
				You offer Robin a pleased smile before explaining. "I may know the reason. I spoke to the <<person1>><<personsimple>> at the popcorn stall, and <<he>> agreed to send thirsty customers your way if you return the favour now and then."
			<<case "flamboyant">>
				You beam at Robin like you're about to unveil a delightful surprise. "Darling, your mystery is solved. I persuaded that popcorn seller to steer thirsty customers to you, provided you send hungry ones back in return."
			<<case "docile">>
				You explain it simply and without fanfare. "I asked the <<person1>><<personsimple>> who sells popcorn to send thirsty customers here. <<He>> only wants you to point hungry people toward <<him>> too."
			<<case "confident">>
				You fold your arms with quiet satisfaction. "Your business is up because I fixed you a partnership. The popcorn seller will send thirsty customers here, and you send hungry ones back to <<him>>."
			<<case "bratty">>
				"Oh, I can tell you exactly why your business is booming," you say, grinning widely. Robin looks at you, wide-eyed and questioning. "It's because I'm a genius, and I convinced that schmuck selling popcorn to send you <<person1>><<his>> thirsty customers. Just send anyone who looks hungry over to <<him>>, and you're square."
			<<case "cruel">>
				You let Robin wonder for a heartbeat longer than necessary before you explain. "I arranged it. The popcorn seller sends thirsty people here, you send hungry ones there, and both of you make more money."
			<<default>>
				"Well," you begin, offering Robin a smile. "You know that stall that sells popcorn? I convinced <<person1>><<him>> to send <<his>> thirsty customers here. <<He>> just wants you to send some customers <<his>> way occasionally too."
		<</switch>>
		<br><br>
		<<balloonRobinGrateful>>

	<<case "confess_sabotaged">>
		<<if _botchedHelp>>
			You take a deep breath and
			<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
				<<case "meek">>
					glance away from Robin. "W-well... I might, um, know the reason," you admit. "I tried to convince that <<person1>><<personsimple>> who sells popcorn to send you <<his>> thirsty customers... but I ended up upsetting <<him>>. I think <<he>> started selling _lemonade in retaliation."
				<<case "shy">>
					stare at the ground for a moment before forcing the words out. "I think this might be my fault. I tried to talk the popcorn seller into sending customers over, but I upset <<person1>><<him>>, and now <<he>>'s selling _lemonade too."
				<<case "polite">>
					address Robin as steadily as you can. "I have some bad news. I tried to persuade the popcorn seller to send thirsty customers your way, but I handled it badly and upset <<person1>><<him>>. <<He>> retaliated by selling <<his>> own _lemonade."
				<<case "flamboyant">>
					let the cheer drain out of your expression. "I know why this is happening, and it's not pretty. I tried to broker a helpful arrangement with the popcorn seller, but I offended <<person1>><<him>> instead. Now <<hes>> selling _lemonade out of spite."
				<<case "docile">>
					speak plainly, without trying to soften it. "I tried to get the popcorn seller to help you, but I upset <<person1>><<him>>. Now <<hes>> selling _lemonade <<himself>>."
				<<case "confident">>
					make yourself meet Robin's eyes. "I know what's going on. I tried to push the popcorn seller into sending customers your way, but I misjudged <<person1>><<him>>. <<He>> took offense and started selling _lemonade to retaliate."
				<<case "bratty">>
					look Robin square in the eye. "I know what's going on. See, I tried to convince that schmuck who sells popcorn to send you <<person1>><<his>> thirsty customers. Accidentally pissed <<him>> off, and <<he>> started selling _lemonade to stick it to me."
				<<case "cruel">>
					say it without flinching. "I tried to manipulate the popcorn seller into helping you. <<person1>><<He>> noticed, got angry, and started selling _lemonade to punish me for it."
				<<default>>
					address Robin. "I have some bad news. You know that stall that sells popcorn? I tried to convince <<person1>><<him>> to send you <<his>> thirsty customers, but it didn't work. I upset <<him>>, and <<he>> retaliated by selling <<his>> own _lemonade."
			<</switch>>
			<br><br>
			Robin looks conflicted. "You're the reason why I'm losing customers?"
		<<else>>
			You take a deep breath and
			<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
				<<case "meek">>
					glance away from Robin. "W-well... I might, um, know the reason," you admit. "It's because I told the <<person1>><<personsimple>> who runs that balloon stand to start selling drinks."
				<<case "shy">>
					struggle through the confession in a rush. "I think I know why. I told the <<person1>><<personsimple>> at the balloon stand to start selling drinks."
				<<case "polite">>
					address Robin carefully. "I think I know why this is happening. I suggested that the <<person1>><<personsimple>> who runs the balloon stand should start selling drinks."
				<<case "flamboyant">>
					force yourself to ruin the mood with the truth. "I know why, darling, and it isn't flattering. I suggested to the balloon seller that <<he>> start serving drinks."
				<<case "docile">>
					admit it plainly. "It's because I told the <<person1>><<personsimple>> who runs the balloon stand to start selling drinks."
				<<case "confident">>
					hold Robin's gaze and own it. "I know why. I was the one who told the balloon seller to start offering drinks."
				<<case "bratty">>
					look Robin square in the eye. "I know what's going on. It's because I told that <<person1>><<personsimple>> who runs the balloon stand to start selling drinks."
				<<case "cruel">>
					confess with brisk precision. "You're losing customers because I suggested your competitor start selling drinks."
				<<default>>
					address Robin. "I think I know why. It's because I told the <<person1>><<personsimple>> who runs that balloon stand to start selling drinks."
			<</switch>>
			<br><br>
			<<person2>><<print C.npc.Robin.trauma gte 20 ? "Robin stares at you hollowly" : C.npc.Robin.dom gte 50 ? "Robin clenches <<his>> fists" : "Tears spring to Robin's eyes, and <<he>> blinks them away">>. <<He>> looks at a loss for words. "You did what?" <<he>> finally whispers. "Why would you do that? It's already hard enough making money without my <<if $robinromance is 1>><<girlfriend "Robin">><<else>>best friend<</if>> giving my competitor ideas. I thought we were in this together."
		<</if>>

	<<case "quiet_helped">>
		You choose to keep quiet. Robin barely notices your silence as <<he>> channels <<his>> giddy energy into rearranging <<his>> ingredients.
		<br><br>
		"Excuse me?" a <<generate3>><<person3>><<person>> interrupts you. "<<print Time.season is "winter" ? "A <<person1>><<personsimple>> at the beach" : "That <<person1>><<personsimple>> over there">> told me you're selling _lemonade? May I buy some?"
		<br><br>
		Robin's eyes widen slightly. "That's where the customers are coming from!" <<person2>><<he>> whispers to you, sounding excited. "What a nice <<person1>><<lady_npc>>... I guess there are good people in this world after all! I should start sending my customers <<his>> way too." Robin starts to make some _lemonade for the <<person3>><<person>>, humming as <<person2>><<he>> goes. <<llrtrauma>><<npcincr Robin trauma -5>><<ggdom Robin>><<npcincr Robin dom 5>>
		<br><br>
		A warm glow fills you as you watch Robin help the customer, oblivious to the role you played. It feels good to do something nice, regardless of public recognition. <<stress -12>><<trauma -6>><<lstress>><<ltrauma>>

	<<case "quiet_sabotaged">>
		You decide not to say anything. Robin doesn't need to know about your <<print ["angry", "appeased"].includes($balloonStand.owner) ? "failure to help <<him>>" : "betrayal">>. Robin fidgets, restlessly rearranging <<his>> ingredients. "Oh well," <<he>> finally says with a sigh. "I guess there's no helping it. I'll just have to keep working hard."
		<br><br>
		You chat for a bit, and Robin seems in slightly better spirits by the time you bid <<him>> farewell.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<if $phase is "confess_sabotaged">>
	<<set $robin.hurtReason to "the balloon stand situation">>
	<<set $robin.timer.hurt to _botchedHelp ? 8 : 15>>
	<<set _trauma to _botchedHelp ? 3 : 6>>
	<<set _robin_trauma to _botchedHelp ? 2 : 15>>
	<<set _robin_love to _botchedHelp ? -1 : -10>>

	<<link [[Apologise|Balloon Robin Check-In 2]]>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>><br>
	<<capture _robin_trauma _robin_love>>
		<<link [[Yell|Balloon Robin Check-In 2]]>><<set $phase to 1>><<trauma -6>><<npcincr Robin trauma _robin_trauma>><<npcincr Robin love _robin_love>><<npcincr Robin dom -1>><</link>><<ltrauma>><<lstress>><<grtrauma>><<llove Robin>><<ldom Robin>><br>
	<</capture>>
	<<capture _trauma>>
		<<link [[Say nothing|Balloon Robin Check-In 2]]>><<set $phase to 2>><<trauma _trauma>><</link>><<gtrauma>><<if !_botchedHelp>><<grtrauma>><</if>>
	<</capture>>
<<else>>
	<<switch $location>>
		<<case "park">><<link [[Next|Park]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
		<<default>><<link [[Next|Beach]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<</switch>>
<</if>>

:: Balloon Robin Check-In 2
<<person2>><<speechresolve>><<effects>>

<<if ["angry", "appeased"].includes($balloonStand.owner)>>
	<<if $phase is 0>>
		<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
			<<case "meek">>
				You shrink a little under Robin's gaze. "I-it was an accident! I'm sorry..." you tell <<person2>><<him>>.
			<<case "shy">>
				You swallow hard before speaking. "I didn't mean for any of this to happen. I'm sorry," you tell <<person2>><<him>>.
			<<case "polite">>
				You keep your voice low and careful. "I handled it badly, and I'm sorry," you tell <<person2>><<him>>.
			<<case "flamboyant">>
				For once, there's no playfulness in your voice. "That was a spectacular mess, and I'm sorry for it," you tell <<person2>><<him>>.
			<<case "docile">>
				You bow your head. "I made a mistake. I'm sorry," you tell <<person2>><<him>>.
			<<case "confident">>
				You force yourself not to look away. "I messed up. I'm sorry," you tell <<person2>><<him>>.
			<<case "bratty">>
				"My bad, alright? I was just trying to help," you tell <<person2>><<him>>.
			<<case "cruel">>
				You keep your expression tight. "I misjudged it. That's on me," you tell <<person2>><<him>>.
			<<default>>
				"I messed up. I'm sorry," you tell <<person2>><<him>>.
		<</switch>>
	<<elseif $phase is 1>>
		You berate Robin, reminding <<person2>><<him>> that you did your best to help. <<He>> <<print C.npc.Robin.dom gte 80 ? "cuts you off before you can get too far in your diatribe" : "hangs <<his>> head as you lay into <<him>>. When you're finished, <<he>> looks up">>.
	<<else>>
		You keep your mouth shut. Robin looks at you balefully before continuing.
	<</if>>
	"I know it's not your fault," Robin says. <<person2>><<He>> <<print C.npc.Robin.dom gte 50 ? "stares at you, <<his>> fists tightly clenched" : "can't quite look you in the eye">>. "Thank you for trying, but <<print C.npc.Robin.dom gte 50 ? "I can take care of myself" : "I think you hurt more than you helped">>." <<He>> sighs. "I just... need some time, okay?"
	<br><br>
<<else>>
	<<if $phase is 0>>
		<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
			<<case "meek">>
				"I-I'm sorry..." you tell <<person2>><<him>>. "I just wanted to help."
			<<case "shy">>
				You twist your hands together. "I'm sorry. I really was trying to help," you tell <<person2>><<him>>.
			<<case "polite">>
				"I'm sorry," you say quietly. "I truly thought I was helping."
			<<case "flamboyant">>
				You wince as the words leave you. "I'm sorry, darling. I thought I was helping, not making everything worse."
			<<case "docile">>
				You lower your eyes. "I'm sorry. I only wanted to help."
			<<case "confident">>
				You hold yourself steady, even if your voice isn't. "I'm sorry. I meant to help, and I got it wrong."
			<<case "bratty">>
				"My bad, alright?" you tell <<person2>><<him>>. "I just wanted to help."
			<<case "cruel">>
				You exhale slowly before answering. "I was trying to help. I know that doesn't excuse it."
			<<default>>
				"I'm sorry," you tell <<person2>><<him>>. "I just wanted to help."
		<</switch>>
		<br><br>
		"Help who? <<person1>><<Him>> or me?" Robin asks. <<person2>><<He>> sounds on the verge of tears. "If you wanted to help me, you should have told <<person1>><<him>> to send people to me for drinks, not to sell <<his>> own."
		<br><br>
		"I'm sorry," you repeat helplessly. "You're right, I shouldn't have done that. I thought maybe..." You break off and shake your head. "I didn't mean to hurt you."
		<br><br>
		"I know." <<person2>><<He>> stares at the ground. "Thank you for wanting to help."
	<<elseif $phase is 1>>
		You raise your voice as you lay into Robin, berating <<him>> for <<his>> naivety. You tell <<him>> that you did <<him>> a favour,
		<<if $robinStand?.selfSufficient is 1>>
			and that paying <<his>> own way doesn't mean <<he>> can afford to let someone else take <<his>> customers.
		<<elseif $robinpaid gte 1>>
			and if <<he>> ever hopes to pay <<his>> own way, <<he>> needs to get a real job.
		<<else>>
			because <<he>> can't make a living just from selling lemonade.
		<</if>>
		By the time you're done, <<hes>> in tears.
		<br><br>
		<<if $robinStand?.selfSufficient is 1>>
			"I'll do better," <<he>> mumbles. "I can take care of my own business..." <<He>> needs a few moments to compose <<himself>>.
		<<else>>
			"I'll do better," <<he>> mumbles, "so you don't have to keep supporting me..." <<He>> needs a few moments to compose <<himself>>.
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		You keep your mouth shut, unable to find the appropriate words.
		<br><br>
		Robin seems even more upset at your reticence. "You can't even tell me why?" <<person2>><<he>> says, voice quivering with tears. <<npcincr Robin trauma 5>><<grtrauma>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	Finally, Robin takes a shuddery breath and swallows. "<<print C.npc.Robin.dom gte 50 ? "I'd like you to leave now" : "P-please, just go">>," <<person2>><<he>> says. "I just... want to be alone right now."
<</if>>

<<He>> turns back to <<his>> stand, avoiding your gaze until you finally leave.
<br><br>

<<switch $location>>
	<<case "park">><<link [[Next|Park]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<<default>><<link [[Next|Beach]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</switch>>

:: Balloon Decline
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>

<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek">>
		You clutch the balloon string and offer an apologetic smile. "Sorry, but I can't right now. Thank you for the free balloon though, that's very kind of you," you say.
	<<case "shy">>
		You hesitate before answering, then give a small shake of your head. "I can't right now, but thank you for the balloon."
	<<case "polite">>
		You decline with a grateful smile. "I can't right now, but thank you. That was very kind of you."
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		You lift the balloon with a light flourish. "Tempting, darling, but I can't right now. Thank you for the lovely freebie."
	<<case "docile">>
		You answer softly and without fuss. "Sorry, I can't right now. Thank you for the balloon."
	<<case "confident">>
		You give the stall a final glance and shake your head. "Not right now, but thanks for the balloon."
	<<case "bratty">>
		"Nah, I'm good. But thanks for the freebie," you say.
	<<case "cruel">>
		You wave the offer off with cool finality. "No. But I'll take the balloon. Thanks."
	<<default>>
		"I'm fine, but thanks for the balloon," you say.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
You take your leave and let the <<person>> finish setting up <<his>> stall.
<br><br>
<<if getRobinLocation() is "beach">>
	<<clearsinglenpc 0>>
	<<balloonRobinIntro>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Balloon Robin Response
<<person2>><<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if $phase is 0>>
	<<set _lemonade to Time.season is "winter" ? "hot chocolate" : "lemonade">>
	<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
		<<case "meek">>
			You reassure Robin as gently as you can, insisting the stall owner isn't selling _lemonade and would probably attract a different sort of customer anyway.
		<<case "shy">>
			You speak up after a small pause, telling Robin that the stall owner isn't selling _lemonade and would likely draw a different crowd.
		<<case "polite">>
			You calmly point out that the stall owner isn't selling _lemonade and would appeal to different customers, so Robin may not have much to worry about.
		<<case "flamboyant">>
			You wave off the concern with a bright little smile, telling Robin that popcorn and _lemonade are hardly the same sort of temptation, and that the stall owner is bound to attract a different crowd.
		<<case "docile">>
			You quietly tell Robin that the stall owner isn't selling _lemonade and would probably pull in different customers.
		<<case "confident">>
			You answer without hesitation. The stall owner isn't selling _lemonade, you point out, and the two stands are likely to draw different people anyway.
		<<case "bratty">>
			You scoff lightly and tell Robin not to overthink it. The stall owner isn't even selling _lemonade, and the two of them would attract different crowds.
		<<case "cruel">>
			You dismiss the worry with clipped certainty. The stall owner isn't selling _lemonade, so the competition isn't as direct as Robin seems to fear.
		<<default>>
			You tell Robin <<he>> has nothing to worry about. The stall owner isn't selling _lemonade and would attract a different crowd.
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>
	"I guess that's true," Robin says. <<He>> glances <<print Time.season is "winter" ? "in the direction of the beach" : "at the stall">>. <<person1>>"<<Hes>> selling popcorn, right? Maybe <<he>>'ll send people over to me if they get thirsty," <<person2>><<he>> says, sounding <<print C.npc.Robin.trauma gte 40 ? "like <<hes>> trying to convince <<himself>> of the impossible" : "hopeful">>.
	<br><br>
	<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
		<<case "meek" "shy" "docile">>
			You nod encouragingly.
		<<case "polite" "flamboyant">>
			You smile and murmur something encouraging.
		<<case "confident">>
			You nod once, like the matter is practically settled.
		<<case "bratty">>
			You grin and tell <<him>> to keep <<his>> chin up.
		<<case "cruel">>
			You tell <<him>> to stay focused and take the chance if it comes.
		<<default>>
			You nod encouragingly.
	<</switch>> <span class="blue">Maybe you can convince the stall owner to help Robin if you purchase some popcorn.</span>
	<br><br>
	The two of you make small talk for a bit. Eventually, Robin says <<he>> needs to get back to <<his>> stand.
	<br>
	<<if C.npc.Robin.trauma gte 40>>
		<<He>> slowly ambles off, <<his>> gaze fixed on the ground.
	<<else>>
		<<He>> smiles and waves goodbye.
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	You don't respond. The silence stretches awkwardly between you. Robin fidgets.
	<br><br>
	"Yeah," <<person2>><<he>> finally says. "I guess maybe I should be worried."
	<<if C.npc.Robin.trauma gte 40>>
		<<He>> sighs, staring vacantly at the stall. "Well, I should get back to it, then." <<He>> slowly ambles off, <<his>> gaze fixed on the ground.
	<<else>>
		<<He>> sighs, looking momentarily despondent before bouncing back to <<his>> usual happy-go-lucky self. "Well, what can you do? I'll just have to keep on working hard." <<He>> smiles and waves goodbye.
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<set $balloonStand.robin.status to "help needed">>
<br><br>
<<switch $location>>
	<<case "park">><<link [[Next|Park]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<<default>><<link [[Next|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</switch>>

:: Balloon Widgets [widget]

<<widget "stallShop-text">>
	<<if (getRobinLocation() is "beach")>>
		<<if $balloonStand.robin.status is "sabotaged">>
			<<set _robinText to "Customers mill around you. Across the way, a harried Robin desperately tries to attract people to <<nnpc_his Robin>> stand.">>
		<<elseif $balloonStand.robin.status is "helped">>
			<<set _robinText to "Across the way, Robin has more customers than usual. <<nnpc_He Robin>> catches you looking and waves at you.">>
		<<else>>
			<<set _robinText to "Across the way, Robin speaks to a solitary customer. <<nnpc_He Robin>> catches you looking and smiles tentatively.">>
		<</if>>
	<<elseif $robinmissing isnot 0>>
		<<if $balloonStand.robin.status is "sabotaged">>
			<<set _robinText to "Customers mill around you. You glance over at the spot where Robin normally set up shop. You can't help but feel responsible for <<nnpc_his Robin>> absence.">>
		<<elseif $balloonStand.robin.status is "helped">>
			<<set _robinText to "The <<personsimple>> begins to point another customer looking for a drink in the direction of Robin's stand. <<He>> quickly corrects <<himself>>, looking dispirited at Robin's absence.">>
		<<else>>
			<<set _robinText to "You glance over at the spot where Robin normally set up shop.">>
		<</if>>
	<<elseif $balloonStand.robin.status is "sabotaged">>
		<<set _robinText to "Customers mill around you.">>
	<<else>>
		<<set _robinText to "">>
	<</if>>

	<<if $phase is "firstcustomer">>
		"Excellent!" The <<person>> claps <<his>> hands in delight. "What would you like?"
	<<else>>
		The <<person>> <<print $balloonStand.owner is "angry" ? "scowls" : "smiles">> at you as you peruse <<his>> stand. The smell of fresh popcorn fills the air. <<print _robinText>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
<</widget>>

<<widget "stallShop-main">>
	<<if $balloonStand.freeDrink>>
		<<set $balloonStand.freeDrink to false>>
		<<switch Time.season>>
			<<case "winter">>
				<<wearProp "travel cup">>
			<<case "spring">>
				<<wearProp "strawberry lemonade">>
			<<case "autumn">>
				<<wearProp "travel cup cider">>
			<<default>>
				<<wearProp "lemonade">>
		<</switch>>

		"Hey, you!" the <<person1>><<person>> says, flashing you a quick smile. "Thanks again for the business idea. I'm already seeing an influx of customers. Here, one drink on the house, as promised."
		<br><br>

		<<if ["autumn", "winter"].includes(Time.season)>>
			You take a careful sip of the offered drink, careful not to scald your tongue. The <<seasonal_beverage>> is rich <<print Time.season is "winter" ? "and creamy" : "with spices">>.
		<<else>>
			You take a sip of the offered drink. The cold <<seasonal_beverage>> is <<print Time.season is "spring" ? "pleasantly fruity" : "tart">> and refreshing.
		<</if>>
		<<stress -9>><<lstress>>
		<br><br>

		You make small talk with the stall owner until a customer interrupts. You thank <<him>> for the free drink and step away.
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>

	<<else>>
		<<if $tryOn.autoReset isnot false>><<tryOnReset>><</if>><<unset $tempDisable>>
		<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
		<<set $shopName = "stall">>
		<<stallShop-text>>

		<div id="tryonstats-div"><<tryOnStats>></div>
		<<unset $shopListStartCount>>
		<<unset $clothes_choice>>
		<<set $shopPage = 0>>

		<div id="warmth-description" class="hidden">
			<<warmthscale>>
			<<warmth_description>>
		</div>

		<<gifticon "balloons">><<link "Browse items">><<replace "#clothingShop-div">><<HandheldShop>><</replace>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>>
		<<run linkifyDivs('.button-back-to-shop')>>
		<<if ndef $popcorn>><<set $popcorn to 0>><</if>>
		<<if ndef $daily.ex.popcorn>><<set $daily.ex.popcorn to 0>><</if>>
		<<if $popcorn gte 3>>
			<br>
			<span class="blue">You can only carry three bags of <<foodicon "popcorn">>popcorn at once.</span>
		<<elseif setup.inflation.canAfford(600) and $daily.ex.popcorn lt 3>>
			<br>
			<<foodicon "popcorn">><<link [[Buy popcorn (0:02 <<printprice 600>>)|Balloon Purchase]]>><<money -600>><<set $phase to "popcorn">><<pass 2>><</link>>
		<</if>>
		<<if $balloonStand.robin.status is "sabotaged" and setup.inflation.canAfford(300) and !($daily.ex.balloonDrink gte 3)>>
			<<switch Time.season>>
				<<case "winter">><<set _drink to "hotcocoa">><<set _phase to "hot cocoa">>
				<<case "spring">><<set _drink to "strawberrylemonade">><<set _phase to "cold drink">>
				<<case "summer">><<set _drink to "lemonade">><<set _phase to "cold drink">>
				<<default>><<set _drink to "hotcider">><<set _phase to "hot cider">>
			<</switch>>
			<br>
			<<foodicon _drink>><<link [[Buy something to drink (0:02 <<printprice 300>>)|Balloon Purchase]]>><<money -300>><<set $phase to _phase>><<set $phase2 to _drink>><<pass 2>><</link>>
		<</if>>
		<<if $balloonStand.robin.status is "convince" and !$daily.ex.balloonConvince>>
			<br>
			<<socialiseicon>><<link [[Persuade the stall owner to partner with Robin|Balloon Convince]]>><<set $phase to "persuade">><</link>><<englishdifficulty 1 1000>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<<if $tryOn.value gt 0>>
			<<if $tryOn.value lte $money>>
				<<sendItemsToDropdown>>
				<<shopicon "register">><<link "Buy items">><<buyTryOnClothes "wear">><<updateclothingshop>><</link>>
				<br>
				<<wardrobeicon>><<link "Buy items and send to wardrobe">>
					<<buyTryOnClothes "wardrobe">>
					<<updatesidebarmoney>>
					<<updatewarmthscale>>
					<<updatewarmthdescription>>
					<<updatesidebarimg>>
					<<updatesidebardescription>>
					<<updateallure>>
					<<updatetryonstats>>
					<<updateclothingshop>>
					<<run updateMoment()>>
				<</link>>
				<br>
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Beach]]>><<shopClothingFilterReset>><<set $tryOn.autoReset to true>><<endevent>><</link>>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "balloonRobinHelped">>
	<<set _boyfriend to ($robinromance ? "<<person2>><<girlfriend_npc>>" : "friend")>>

	"You're either <<print $robinromance ? "really in love with <<person2>><<him>>" : "a really good friend">>, or you really believe in the quality of <<person2>><<his>> stuff. Either way, I'll take it. Sure, we've got a deal. I'll send my customers to your _boyfriend's stall, if <<he>>'ll send any peckish customers my way."

	<<set $robin.moneyModifier += 50>>
	<<set $balloonStand.robin.status to "helped">>
	<<set $robin.timer.customer to 5>> /*Give Robin a few days to notice the effects on their stall*/
<</widget>>

<<widget "balloonRobinSabotaged">>
	<<set $robin.moneyModifier -= 50>>
	<<set $balloonStand.robin.status to "sabotaged">>
	<<set $balloonStand.owner to _args[0] or "friendly">>
	<<set $robin.timer.customer to 5>> /*Give Robin a few days to notice the effects on their stall*/
	<<set $daily.ex.balloonDrink to 3>> /*So the balloon owner doesn't start selling lemonade three seconds after*/
<</widget>>

<<widget "balloonRobinGrateful">>
	<<set _boyfriend to ($robinromance ? "<<person2>><<girlfriend_npc>>" : "best friend")>>
	<<set _lemonade to Time.season is "winter" ? "hot chocolate" : "lemonade">>
	<<set _stall to Time.season is "winter" ? "A <<person1>><<personsimple>> at the beach" : "That <<person1>><<personsimple>> over there">>

	Robin's mouth gapes for a few seconds. "You... did that for me?"
	<br><br>
	"Of course I did," you say. "You're my _boyfriend."
	<br><br>
	Robin looks at you for a moment before flinging <<person2>><<his>> arms around your neck and
	<<if $robinromance is 1>>
		kissing you. <<takeKissVirginity "Robin" "loveInterest">>
		<<if _pcKissVirginityTaken>>
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
		<<He>> breaks away with a gasp, looking flustered.
	<<else>>
		hugging you hard enough to hurt. <<He>> breaks away first, visibly choked up.
	<</if>>
	There's tears in <<his>> eyes as <<he>> whispers, "Thank you. You do so much for me... what would I do without you?" <<He>> hugs you <<print $robinromance is 1 ? "tenderly" : "again">>, and the two of you stay like that for a moment.
	<br><br>
	"Excuse me?" a <<generate3>><<person3>><<person>> interrupts your embrace. "<<print _stall>> told me you're selling _lemonade? May I buy some?"
	<<if $location isnot "park">>
		<br><br>
		You glance over at the balloon stall. The <<person>> gives you a wink.
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	"Ah, of course!" Robin says. "I'll make you some right now, <<person3>><<sir>>!" <<person2>><<He>> gives you one last grateful smile and busies <<himself>> with the _lemonade. <<ggglove "Robin">><<llrtrauma>><<npcincr Robin trauma -10>><<npcincr Robin love 10>>
	<br><br>
	A warm glow fills you. You watch Robin help the customer before bidding <<him>> farewell. <<He>> mouths you one last grateful "thank you" before you leave. <<famegood 5>><<stress -3>><<trauma -3>><<lstress>><<ltrauma>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "balloonRobinAngryHelp">>
	"I'm okay. I don't need <<print ["angry", "appeased"].includes($balloonStand.owner) ? "any more of your" : "your">> help right now." Robin fidgets. "Would you mind leaving me alone for a few?" It's clear <<hes>> still <<npcHurt "Robin">>.
	<br><br>
	<<endevent>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "balloonRobinAngryPurchase">>
	"Thanks for your purchase," <<he>> says. <<He>> seems to feel bad about being icy towards you, and <<his>> face softens as <<he>> puts the money under the counter.
<</widget>>

<<widget "balloonRobinTalk">>
	Robin glances at you.
	<<if $balloonStand.robin.status is "helped" and $balloonStand.robin.talked is false and $robin.timer.customer is 0>>
		"I don't know if you've noticed, but I've been getting so many more customers lately!" <<He>> looks pleased, if a bit flustered. "I don't know what's causing it, but... wow!"
	<<elseif $balloonStand.robin.status is "sabotaged" and $balloonStand.robin.talked is false and $robin.timer.customer is 0>>
		"You know, I haven't been getting a lot of customers lately." <<His>> expression clouds over. "That stall <<print getRobinLocation() is "beach" ? "over there started selling lemonade" : "on the beach with the popcorn and balloons started selling <<seasonal_beverage>>">>..." <<He>> sighs. "I wish I knew why."
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "balloonRobinIntro">>
	<<loadNPC 0 "stall_owner">><<npc Robin 2>><<person2>>
	<<set _lemonade to Time.season is "winter" ? "hot chocolate" : "lemonade">>

	You see Robin stood behind <<his>> _lemonade stand. When <<he>> notices you, <<he>> leaves the stand and
	<<if C.npc.Robin.trauma gte 40>>
		shuffles over to you. "Hey," <<he>> mumbles. "Have you... <<print Time.season is "winter" ? "heard about that stall on the beach" : "seen that stall over there">>? The one selling the balloons and popcorn. Should I be worried? It's already hard enough to find customers."
	<<else>>
		approaches you. "Hey, I'm happy to see you here! I hope you'll stop by the stand later." Robin chews <<his>> lip. "Have you seen that other stall that's set up shop <<print Time.season is "winter" ? "on the beach" : "here">>? Should I be worried? I don't want my customers getting distracted by popcorn!"
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Reassure Robin|Balloon Robin Response]]>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>><br>
	<<link [[Say nothing|Balloon Robin Response]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
<</widget>>
